# Class Properties and Constructors 🏗️

In TypeScript, class fields must be declared with types:

```typescript
class Account {
  id: string;
  balance: number;

  constructor(id: string, initialBalance: number = 0) {
    this.id = id;
    this.balance = initialBalance;
  }

  deposit(amount: number): number {
    this.balance += amount;
    return this.balance;
  }
}

const myAccount = new Account("ACC-101", 500);
myAccount.deposit(250);
console.log(`Account ${myAccount.id} Balance: $${myAccount.balance}`);
```

