# Parameter Properties: The Super Shorthand ⚡

Tired of declaring a property, accepting it in the constructor, and writing `this.x = x`?

Add an access modifier directly to the constructor parameters! TypeScript **automatically declares and assigns the property** for you:

```typescript
// All in one line!
class Developer {
  constructor(
    public name: string,
    public role: string,
    private salary: number
  ) {}

  printInfo() {
    console.log(`${this.name} works as a ${this.role}`);
  }
}

const dev = new Developer("Elena", "Full Stack Engineer", 120000);
dev.printInfo();
```

