# Readonly Class Properties 🔒

Mark properties as `readonly` to prevent mutation after constructor initialization:

```typescript
class ServerConfig {
  readonly ipAddress: string;
  readonly port: number;

  constructor(ip: string, port: number) {
    this.ipAddress = ip;
    this.port = port;
  }
}

const server = new ServerConfig("192.168.1.1", 8080);
// server.port = 9000; // Error: Cannot assign to 'port' because it is a read-only property!
console.log(`Server running at ${server.ipAddress}:${server.port}`);
```

