# The `implements` Keyword 🤝

Classes can implement one or more interfaces to guarantee compliance with API contracts:

```typescript
interface Logger {
  log(message: string): void;
}

interface Clearable {
  clear(): void;
}

class ConsoleLogger implements Logger, Clearable {
  log(msg: string): void {
    console.log(`[LOG]: ${msg}`);
  }

  clear(): void {
    console.log("Log buffer cleared.");
  }
}

const logger = new ConsoleLogger();
logger.log("System operational");
logger.clear();
```

