# TypeScript `private` vs JavaScript `#private` ⚖️

- **TypeScript `private`:** Enforced **only at compile time**. At runtime after compilation to JavaScript, the property becomes public!
- **ECMAScript `#private`:** Enforced by the **JavaScript engine itself at runtime**. It is truly inaccessible even via `Object.keys()` or reflection!

```typescript
class SecretKeeper {
  private tsPrivate = "Compile-time only";
  #jsPrivate = "True hard runtime privacy";

  reveal() {
    console.log(this.#jsPrivate);
  }
}

const keeper = new SecretKeeper();
keeper.reveal();
```

