# Design Patterns: The Singleton Pattern 🛡️

Ensure a class has only one single instance across your entire application using a `private constructor`:

```typescript
class AppConfig {
  private static instance: AppConfig;
  public theme: string = "dark";

  // Private constructor prevents calling 'new AppConfig()' externally!
  private constructor() {}

  static getInstance(): AppConfig {
    if (!AppConfig.instance) {
      AppConfig.instance = new AppConfig();
    }
    return AppConfig.instance;
  }
}

const c1 = AppConfig.getInstance();
const c2 = AppConfig.getInstance();
console.log("Are both instances identical?", c1 === c2); // true!
```

